        "v": 5,
        "title": "Claude API retry logic added",
        "summary": "Backend now retries `promptClaudeStream` up to 3 times on `APIConnectionError` with exponential backoff. Other Anthropic errors propagate immediately with user-facing support email. WebSocket error display strips redundant `Error: ` prefix. Files: `backend/src/claude.ts`, `backend/src/websockets/websocket-action.ts`.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:55:38.416Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the system talks to Claude and the connection drops, it now tries again a few times instead of giving up right away. If Claude returns a different kind of error, that message now skips the retry and goes straight to you with the support team's email so you know who to contact. Error messages you see in your browser no longer start with a duplicated 'Error: ' label. Live today.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
