        "title": "WebSocket middleware quota and halt logs downgrade to warn",
        "summary": "Three logger.error calls in backend/src/websockets/middleware.ts switched to logger.warn. Covers middleware execution halts and quota exceeded events for both user and fingerprint. Internal log severity adjustment in WebSocket middleware.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:55:30.236Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Behind the scenes, the system quietly lowered the urgency flag on three internal alerts that were previously treated as errors. These alerts fire when the connection-handling layer stops early or when usage limits are hit for individual accounts or devices. Nothing you can see changes for you today; the same limits apply, the same early stops happen, and only the internal log book now marks those moments as warnings instead of errors. If you happen to peek into server logs, you’ll notice the red error tags are gone, swapped for softer yellow warning notes.",
